<h1 id=3D"rfcnum">RFC 9562</h1>
<h1 id=3D"title">Universally Unique IDentifiers (UUIDs)</h1>
<section id=3D"section-abstract">
      <h2 id=3D"abstract"><a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562=
.html#abstract" class=3D"selfRef">Abstract</a></h2>
<p id=3D"section-abstract-1">This specification defines UUIDs (Universally =
Unique IDentifiers) --
      also known as GUIDs (Globally Unique IDentifiers) -- and a Uniform
      Resource Name namespace for UUIDs. A UUID is 128 bits long and is int=
ended to
      guarantee uniqueness across space and time.  UUIDs were originally us=
ed
      in the Apollo Network Computing System (NCS), later in the Open Softw=
are
      Foundation's (OSF's) Distributed Computing Environment (DCE), and the=
n
      in Microsoft Windows platforms.<a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/=
rfc/rfc9562.html#section-abstract-1" class=3D"pilcrow">=C2=B6</a></p>
<p id=3D"section-abstract-2">This specification is derived from the OSF DCE=
 specification with the
      kind permission of the OSF (now known as "The Open Group").  Informat=
ion
      from earlier versions of the OSF DCE specification have been incorpor=
ated
      into this document. This document obsoletes RFC 4122.<a href=3D"https=
://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#section-abstract-2" class=3D"pilcrow=
">=C2=B6</a></p>
</section>
