org/rfc/rfc9562.html#section-2.1-6.16" class=3D"pilcrow">=C2=B6</a>
</li>
        </ol>
<p id=3D"section-2.1-7">An inspection of these implementations and the issu=
es described
        above has led to this document, in which new UUIDs are adapted to
        address these issues.<a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9=
562.html#section-2.1-7" class=3D"pilcrow">=C2=B6</a></p>
<p id=3D"section-2.1-8">Further, <span>[<a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.o=
rg/rfc/rfc9562.html#RFC4122" class=3D"cite xref">RFC4122</a>]</span> itself=
 was in need of an overhaul to
        address a number of topics such as, but not limited to, the
        following:<a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#se=
ction-2.1-8" class=3D"pilcrow">=C2=B6</a></p>
<ol start=3D"1" type=3D"1" class=3D"normal type-1" id=3D"section-2.1-9">
   <li id=3D"section-2.1-9.1">Implementation of miscellaneous errata report=
s. Mostly around
   bit-layout clarifications, which lead to inconsistent
   implementations <span>[<a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562=
.html#Err1957" class=3D"cite xref">Err1957</a>]</span>, <span>[<a href=3D"h=
ttps://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#Err3546" class=3D"cite xref">Err=
3546</a>]</span>,
   <span>[<a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#Err4975" c=
lass=3D"cite xref">Err4975</a>]</span>, <span>[<a href=3D"https://www.rfc-e=
ditor.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#Err4976" class=3D"cite xref">Err4976</a>]</span>=
, <span>[<a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#Err5560" cl=
ass=3D"cite xref">Err5560</a>]</span>, etc.<a href=3D"https://www.rfc-edito=
r.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#section-2.1-9.1" class=3D"pilcrow">=C2=B6</a>
</li>
          <li id=3D"section-2.1-9.2">Decoupling other UUID versions from th=
e UUIDv1 bit layout so that
          fields like "time_hi_and_version" do not need to be referenced
          within a UUID that is not time based while also providing
          definition sections similar to that for UUIDv1 for UUIDv3, UUIDv4=
, and UUIDv5.<a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#section=
-2.1-9.2" class=3D"pilcrow">=C2=B6</a>
</li>
          <li id=3D"section-2.1-9.3">Providing implementation best practice=
s around many real-world
          scenarios and corner cases observed by existing and prototype
          implementations.<a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562=
.html#section-2.1-9.3" class=3D"pilcrow">=C2=B6</a>
</li>
          <li id=3D"section-2.1-9.4">Addressing security best practices and
          considerations for the modern age as it pertains to MAC addresses=
,
          hashing algorithms, secure randomness, and other topics.<a href=
=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#section-2.1-9.4" class=3D"p=
ilcrow">=C2=B6</a>
</li>
          <li id=3D"section-2.1-9.5">Providing implementations a standard-b=
ased option for
          implementation-specific and/or experimental UUID designs.<a href=
=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#section-2.1-9.5" class=3D"p=
ilcrow">=C2=B6</a>
</li>
          <li id=3D"section-2.1-9.6">Providing more test vectors that illus=
trate real UUIDs created as
          per the specification.<a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/r=
fc9562.html#section-2.1-9.6" class=3D"pilcrow">=C2=B6</a>
</li>
        </ol>
</section>
