<p id=3D"section-4.1-4">Interoperability, in any form, with variants other =
than the one
defined here is not guaranteed but is not likely to be an issue in
practice.<a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#section-4.1=
-4" class=3D"pilcrow">=C2=B6</a></p>
<p id=3D"section-4.1-5">Specifically for UUIDs in this document, bits 64 an=
d 65 of the UUID (bits 0 and 1 of octet 8) <span class=3D"bcp14">MUST</span=
> be set to 1 and 0 as specified in row 2 of <a href=3D"https://www.rfc-edi=
tor.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#table1" class=3D"auto internal xref">Table 1</a>.
Accordingly, all bit and field layouts avoid the use of these bits.<a href=
=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#section-4.1-5" class=3D"pil=
crow">=C2=B6</a></p>
</section>
</div>
<div id=3D"version_field">
<section id=3D"section-4.2">
        <h3 id=3D"name-version-field">
<a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#section-4.2" class=
=3D"section-number selfRef">4.2. </a><a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/=
rfc/rfc9562.html#name-version-field" class=3D"section-name selfRef">Version=
 Field</a>
        </h3>
<p id=3D"section-4.2-1">The version number is in the most significant 4 bit=
s of octet 6
(bits 48 through 51 of the UUID).<a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/=
rfc9562.html#section-4.2-1" class=3D"pilcrow">=C2=B6</a></p>
