<div id=3D"iana3">
<section id=3D"section-7.2">
        <h3 id=3D"name-iana-uuid-namespace-id-regi">
<a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#section-7.2" class=
=3D"section-number selfRef">7.2. </a><a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/=
rfc/rfc9562.html#name-iana-uuid-namespace-id-regi" class=3D"section-name se=
lfRef">IANA UUID Namespace ID Registry and Registration</a>
        </h3>
<p id=3D"section-7.2-1">This specification defines the "UUID Namespace IDs"=
 registry for common, widely used Namespace ID values.<a href=3D"https://ww=
w.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#section-7.2-1" class=3D"pilcrow">=C2=B6</=
a></p>
<p id=3D"section-7.2-2">The full details of this registration, including in=
formation for designated experts, can be found in <a href=3D"https://www.rf=
c-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#namespaces" class=3D"auto internal xref">Sect=
ion 6.6</a>.<a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#section-=
7.2-2" class=3D"pilcrow">=C2=B6</a></p>
</section>
</div>
</section>
</div>
<div id=3D"Security">
<section id=3D"section-8">
      <h2 id=3D"name-security-considerations">
<a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#section-8" class=3D"=
section-number selfRef">8. </a><a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rf=
c9562.html#name-security-considerations" class=3D"section-name selfRef">Sec=
urity Considerations</a>
      </h2>
<p id=3D"section-8-1">Implementations <span class=3D"bcp14">SHOULD NOT</spa=
n> assume that UUIDs are hard
      to guess.  For example, they <span class=3D"bcp14">MUST NOT</span> be=
 used as security
      capabilities (identifiers whose mere possession grants access).
      Discovery of predictability in a random number source will result in =
a
      vulnerability.<a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#=
section-8-1" class=3D"pilcrow">=C2=B6</a></p>
<p id=3D"section-8-2">Implementations <span class=3D"bcp14">MUST NOT</span>=
 assume that it is easy to
      determine if a UUID has been slightly modified in order to redirect a
      reference to another object.  Humans do not have the ability to easil=
y
      check the integrity of a UUID by simply glancing at it.<a href=3D"htt=
ps://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#section-8-2" class=3D"pilcrow">=C2=
=B6</a></p>
<p id=3D"section-8-3">MAC addresses pose inherent security risks around pri=
vacy and
      <span class=3D"bcp14">SHOULD NOT</span> be used within a UUID.  Inste=
ad CSPRNG data
      <span class=3D"bcp14">SHOULD</span> be selected from a source with su=
fficient entropy
      to ensure guaranteed uniqueness among UUID generation. See Sections
      <a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#unguessability=
" class=3D"auto internal xref">6.9</a> and <a href=3D"https://www.rfc-edito=
r.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#unidentifiable" class=3D"auto internal xref">6.10</a=
> for more information.<a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562.ht=
ml#section-8-3" class=3D"pilcrow">=C2=B6</a></p>
<p id=3D"section-8-4">Timestamps embedded in the UUID do pose a very small =
attack
      surface. The timestamp in conjunction with an embedded counter does
      signal the order of creation for a given UUID and its corresponding d=
ata
      but does not define anything about the data itself or the application=
 as
      a whole.  If UUIDs are required for use with any security operation
      within an application context in any shape or form, then UUIDv4 (<a h=
ref=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#uuidv4" class=3D"auto in=
ternal xref">Section 5.4</a>) <span class=3D"bcp14">SHOULD</span> be utiliz=
ed.<a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#section-8-4" clas=
s=3D"pilcrow">=C2=B6</a></p>
<p id=3D"section-8-5">See <span>[<a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/=
rfc9562.html#RFC6151" class=3D"cite xref">RFC6151</a>]</span> for MD5 secur=
ity considerations and
      <span>[<a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#RFC6194=
" class=3D"cite xref">RFC6194</a>]</span> for SHA-1 security considerations=
.<a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#section-8-5" class=
=3D"pilcrow">=C2=B6</a></p>
</section>
</div>
