<div id=3D"ill_examples">
<section id=3D"appendix-B">
      <h2 id=3D"name-illustrative-examples">
<a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#appendix-B" class=3D=
"section-number selfRef">Appendix B. </a><a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.=
org/rfc/rfc9562.html#name-illustrative-examples" class=3D"section-name self=
Ref">Illustrative Examples</a>
      </h2>
<p id=3D"appendix-B-1">The following sections contain illustrative examples=
 that serve to
      show how one may use UUIDv8 (<a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rf=
c/rfc9562.html#uuidv8" class=3D"auto internal xref">Section 5.8</a>) for cu=
stom and/or
      experimental application-based logic.  The examples below have not be=
en
      through the same rigorous testing, prototyping, and feedback loop tha=
t
      other algorithms in this document have undergone.  The authors
      encourage implementers to create their own UUIDv8 algorithm rather th=
an
      use the items defined in this section.<a href=3D"https://www.rfc-edit=
or.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#appendix-B-1" class=3D"pilcrow">=C2=B6</a></p>
<div id=3D"uuidv8_example">
<section id=3D"appendix-B.1">
        <h3 id=3D"name-example-of-a-uuidv8-value-t">
<a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#appendix-B.1" class=
=3D"section-number selfRef">B.1. </a><a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/=
rfc/rfc9562.html#name-example-of-a-uuidv8-value-t" class=3D"section-name se=
lfRef">Example of a UUIDv8 Value (Time-Based)</a>
        </h3>
<p id=3D"appendix-B.1-1">This example UUIDv8 test vector utilizes a well-kn=
own 64-bit Unix
        Epoch timestamp with 10 ns precision, truncated to the
        least significant, rightmost bits to fill the first 60 bits of
        custom_a and custom_b, while setting the version bits between these=
 two
        segments to the version value of 8.<a href=3D"https://www.rfc-edito=
r.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#appendix-B.1-1" class=3D"pilcrow">=C2=B6</a></p>
<p id=3D"appendix-B.1-2">The variant bits are set; and the final segment, c=
ustom_c, is filled
        with random data.<a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562.=
html#appendix-B.1-2" class=3D"pilcrow">=C2=B6</a></p>
<p id=3D"appendix-B.1-3">Timestamp is Tuesday, February 22, 2022 2:22:22.00=
0000 PM
        GMT-05:00, represented as 0x2489E9AD2EE2E00 or 164555774200000000
        (10 ns-steps).<a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562.htm=
l#appendix-B.1-3" class=3D"pilcrow">=C2=B6</a></p>
<span id=3D"name-uuidv8-example-time-based-i"></span><figure id=3D"figure-2=
7">
          <div class=3D"alignLeft art-text artwork" id=3D"appendix-B.1-4.1"=
>
<pre>-------------------------------------------
field     bits value
-------------------------------------------
custom_a  48   0x2489E9AD2EE2
ver        4   0x8
custom_b  12   0xE00
var        2   0b10
custom_c  62   0b00, 0xEC932D5F69181C0
-------------------------------------------
total     128
-------------------------------------------
final: 2489E9AD-2EE2-8E00-8EC9-32D5F69181C0
</pre>
</div>
<figcaption><a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#figure-2=
7" class=3D"selfRef">Figure 27</a>:
<a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#name-uuidv8-example-=
time-based-i" class=3D"selfRef">UUIDv8 Example Time-Based Illustrative Exam=
ple</a>
          </figcaption></figure>
</section>
</div>
<div id=3D"uuidv8_example_name">
<section id=3D"appendix-B.2">
        <h3 id=3D"name-example-of-a-uuidv8-value-n">
<a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#appendix-B.2" class=
=3D"section-number selfRef">B.2. </a><a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/=
rfc/rfc9562.html#name-example-of-a-uuidv8-value-n" class=3D"section-name se=
lfRef">Example of a UUIDv8 Value (Name-Based)</a>
        </h3>
<p id=3D"appendix-B.2-1">As per <a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/r=
fc9562.html#uuidv5" class=3D"auto internal xref">Section 5.5</a>, name-base=
d UUIDs that want to use
        modern hashing algorithms <span class=3D"bcp14">MUST</span> be crea=
ted within the
        UUIDv8 space. These <span class=3D"bcp14">MAY</span> leverage newer=
 hashing
        algorithms such as SHA-256 or SHA-512 (as defined by <span>[<a href=
=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#FIPS180-4" class=3D"cite xr=
ef">FIPS180-4</a>]</span>), SHA-3 or SHAKE (as defined by <span>[<a href=3D=
"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#FIPS202" class=3D"cite xref">F=
IPS202</a>]</span>), or even algorithms that have not been defined
        yet.<a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#appendix=
-B.2-1" class=3D"pilcrow">=C2=B6</a></p>
<p id=3D"appendix-B.2-2">A SHA-256 version of the SHA-1 computation in <a h=
ref=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#uuidv5_example" class=3D=
"auto internal xref">Appendix A.4</a> is detailed in <a href=3D"https://www=
.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#v8sha256" class=3D"auto internal xref">Fig=
ure 28</a> as
        an illustrative example detailing how this can be achieved.  The
        creation of the name-based UUIDv8 value in this section follows the
        same logic defined in <a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc=
9562.html#uuidv5" class=3D"auto internal xref">Section 5.5</a> with the dif=
ference
        being SHA-256 in place of SHA-1.<a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.o=
rg/rfc/rfc9562.html#appendix-B.2-2" class=3D"pilcrow">=C2=B6</a></p>
<p id=3D"appendix-B.2-3">The field mapping and all values are illustrated i=
n <a href=3D"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9562.html#v8fieldssha256" cl=
ass=3D"auto internal xref">Figure 29</a>.  Finally, to further illustrate t=
he bit
        swapping for version and variant and the unused/discarded part of t=
he
